  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "Nguni 'hour + ordinal' construction: hours are class-5 ordinals (lokuqala, lesibili, ..., letshumi lambili), patterns 'ihola {h}' + additive minutes with Ndebele 'la-' linking ('ihola lesibili lemizuzu emihlanu'), :30 = 'lengxenye' (the file's own half word). Additive forms for :35-:55 to avoid an uncertain 'to' construction. Compromises: used 'ihola' (Zimbabwean Ndebele word for hour) while the file's duration section uses Zulu-style 'ihora'; class-4 minute concords (emihlanu, elitshumi, engamatshumi ...) are my best reconstruction and need native review. Digit fallback is the safe alternative if this is rejected."
    }
  ]
